 "headlines": [
  "<b>AVGO</b> is the one to watch. It's inside a flip zone that has been moving ($331\u2013351), under its largest $360 level (+7.4K). Support at $332.5 is weak; below that there's none around $340. It's net negative into opex (\u221236.2K), so swings are likely to be bigger.",
  "<b>AAPL</b> has the most positioning into opex (+298K), centred on $360\u2013365.",
  "<b>GOOGL</b> is on its $292 flip but net negative into opex (\u221215.4K), so swings are likely to be bigger. <b>TSLA</b> faces resistance at $400 (and it's sitting on its $375\u2013394 flip zone), and <b>AMZN</b> at $270\u2013275 (and it's sitting on its $264 flip).",
  "<b>TSM</b> closed below its flip ($397), with net negative positioning into opex, so moves can run until it gets back above.",
  "Looking to the 12/18 opex, <b>AAPL</b> has the most positioning (+151K); <b>NVDA</b>, <b>AVGO</b>, and <b>TSM</b> stay net negative into both opex dates; <b>GOOGL</b> flips from negative this month to positive.",
  "<b>NVDA</b> is the weakest board, at \u2212176K into opex. It's below its $163\u2013174 flip zone, and TradeEcho rates it 2/5."
